    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math education by adapting explanations to individual learning levels, like mine (lower secondary). They can break down complex problems into simpler steps, provide instant feedback, and make abstract concepts more relatable. For universities, they could assist with advanced topics while ensuring accessibility for diverse learners."
